+# Phase 2.5 status
+
+The harness is incomplete. Real source instrumentation, the regression fixtures, apply/cleanup scripts, the guarded build/run/collection entry point and the Phase 3 guide are present. There are no collected implementation traces and no trace-validation result.
+
+The independent v1 review found four material issues. The proposed correction moves imports after inner documentation, captures the false park-check end directly after its load, and adds same-interface consumers and an observer/consumer fixture. Exact-version re-review is pending. The clock issue remains open: unfenced TSC reads and sample handshakes do not establish the operation intervals required by this TraceSpec. The gate blocks dependent execution and grouped trace production until the controller supplies an admissible method and obtains independent approval.
+
+The host's observed available memory has also remained below the resource policy's 10 GiB kernel-build threshold. Each `run.sh` attempt records a fresh reading. The controller owns admission and the held heavy-stage lock. This worker has not reacquired it or launched another pipeline phase.
+
+| Evidence | Disposition |
+| --- | --- |
+| Source pin and 23 contract-file hashes | Verified before instrumentation. |
+| Initial v1 C fixture, Linux and Asterinas compile variants | Compiled in the pinned project container. These are prior-version binaries, not proof of the corrected candidate. |
+| Corrected scripts | Python AST and Bash syntax checked. Apply idempotence and `git diff --check` passed. |
+| Post-state checks | All 41 decoder names match exact TraceSpec arms. This is static L2 inspection. |
+| Corrected Rust and C build | `NOT_RUN`. |
+| Linux runtime control, WR-SQ and WR-CF | `NOT_RUN`. |
+| Asterinas guest, actual guest SMP and schedule evidence | `NOT_RUN`. |
+| Event coverage, timebox overlap and trace validation | `NOT_RUN`. |
+| Confirmation, classification and repair | Not invoked. They are outside this worker's assigned phase. |
+
+Every priority question retains a separate disposition:
+
+1. Unique consumption and post-reap results have hooks and prepared same/mixed-interface fixtures. No runtime result exists.
+2. Repeated WNOWAIT and late retained observation have prepared fixtures and distinct selection/removal/output hooks. The late-return schedule is not demonstrated.
+3. Registration, recheck, both wake paths, token handling, park/dequeue/resume and second-consumer ECHILD have hooks. WR-09/10 windows and completion remain unobserved. A watchdog alone would not establish a lost wakeup.
+4. Exit-code store, zombie publication, Acquire observation, retained status reads and copyout have separate hooks. The clock ordering prerequisite remains unresolved, and no visibility claim is established.
+5. No-event and post-reap outputs are prepared, with separate poisoned-output and copyout-fault controls. WR-SQ remains a source lead, and WR-CF remains uncalibrated at runtime.
+
+Preserve `evidence/candidate-v1`, its review, the proposed candidate, exact diffs and execution receipts. Continue this campaign after the clock review and resource admission are closed. Do not report Phase 2.5 as passed or use the spec-generation synthetic fixtures as implementation traces.
